n_Down_Long_Barrows]; The north-western barrow is 2.4 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thickthorn_Down_Long_Barrows]; The south-eastern barrow is also 2.4 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thickthorn_Down_Long_Barrows]; One of the two barrows is still unexcavated [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thickthorn_Down_Long_Barrows]; The north-western barrow is aligned north-west to south-east [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thickthorn_Down_Long_Barrows]; The south-eastern barrow is also aligned north-west to south-east (so both are) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thickthorn_Down_Long_Barrows]"}]'::jsonb),
