 Makra Stoa', 'c6cc3a46416247b24bab432c53c3cef6169c035bcfc361fbf0bce0f6d1a5fef6', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-025", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Built in the time of Pericles, the long Makra Stoa stored imported barley and wheat for Athens, supplied its fleet of triremes and, in times of shortage, fed the people directly."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-025 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "it was built in the time of Pericles [S1]; the Makra Stoa was a long building [S3]; it stored imported barley and wheat [S3]; the grain went to Athens [S4]; it supplied the Athenian fleet of triremes [S5]; in times of shortage it supplied the people directly [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-075 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Makra Stoa is an archaeological site, a long stoa that formed part of the ancient city of Piraeus, the port of Athens [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]; The Makra Stoa was built in the time of Pericles [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]; The Makra Stoa was a long building that stored imported barley and wheat [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]; The grain stored there was sent on to Athens for consumption [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]; The stoa supplied the Athenian fleet of triremes [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]; In times of shortage the stoa supplied the people directly [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makra_Stoa]"}]'::jsonb),
