06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Above Marsaxlokk Bay, Tas-Silġ holds remains covering 4000 years: a Megalithic temple, a Phoenician and Punic sanctuary to Astarte, and a Roman complex to Juno mentioned by Cicero."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-026 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site lies above Marsaxlokk Bay [S1]; the remains cover 4000 years [S2]; there is a Megalithic temple [S3]; there is a Phoenician and Punic sanctuary to Astarte [S3]; in Roman times the site was a complex dedicated to Juno [S4]; the site is mentioned by Cicero [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-077 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Tas-Silġ is a multi-period sanctuary (temple) site on a hilltop in Malta [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; The site lies above (overlooks) Marsaxlokk Bay [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; The site holds remains covering 4000 years [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; The site includes a Megalithic temple [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; The site includes a Phoenician and Punic sanctuary to Astarte [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; In the Roman era the site was a religious complex dedicated to Juno [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]; The Roman temple of Juno is mentioned by Cicero [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tas-Sil%C4%A1]"}]'::jsonb),
