s-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Upstream of the Gorges du Verdon, Castellane keeps traces of Neolithic nomads dating back to 6000 BC. Later, the Suetrii built an oppidum named Ducelia and mined salt to sell."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-026 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Castellane lies upstream of the Gorges du Verdon [S1]; Neolithic nomads came through the area [S3]; the traces date back to 6000 BC [S3]; the Suetrii later created an oppidum [S5]; the oppidum was named Ducelia [S5]; they mined salt in the area and sold it [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-078 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Castellane is a town (a commune) in France [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; Castellane lies upstream of the Gorges du Verdon [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; Neolithic nomads came through the Castellane area [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; The oldest traces of these Neolithic nomads date back to 6000 BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; The Suetrii later built an oppidum near Castellane [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; The oppidum was named Ducelia [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]; The Suetrii mined salt in the area and sold it [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castellane]"}]'::jsonb),
